 paths←folder GetPathsInCommits(filename hashes);rc;msg;buff;groups;log;hash;ind;i;j
⍝ Returns, for every commit in `hashes`, the path `filename` had in that commit, so that
⍝ `git show hash:path` works even when the file was renamed since then.\\
⍝ `filename` is relative to the root of the project and names the file as it is known now.\\
⍝ Git does not record renames; `git log --follow` detects them, and lists every commit that
⍝ changed the file together with the path the file had in that commit. A commit that did not
⍝ change the file gets the path of the most recent such commit that is one of its ancestors.\\
⍝ When a path cannot be established `filename` itself is returned: `git show` then reports
⍝ the problem.
 paths←(≢hashes)⍴⊂filename
 (rc msg buff)←folder RunGitCommand'-c core.quotepath=off log --follow --name-only --format="⍙%H" -- "',filename,'"'
 buff←(0<≢¨buff)/buff
 :If 0=rc
 :AndIf 0<≢buff
     groups←(+\'⍙'=⊃¨buff)⊆buff                ⍝ One group per commit: its hash, then the path
     groups←(1<≢¨groups)/groups
     log←{(1↓⊃⍵)(⊃⌽⍵)}¨groups                   ⍝ (fullHash path), most recent commit first
     :For i :In ⍳≢hashes
         hash←i⊃hashes
         :If 0<≢ind←⍸(⊂hash)≡¨(≢hash)↑¨⊃¨log
             (i⊃paths)←2⊃(⊃ind)⊃log
         :Else
             :For j :In ⍳≢log
                 :If 0=⊃folder RunGitCommand'merge-base --is-ancestor ',(1⊃j⊃log),' ',hash
                     (i⊃paths)←2⊃j⊃log
                     :Leave
                 :EndIf
             :EndFor
         :EndIf
     :EndFor
 :EndIf
⍝Done
